UID:57ku4dntd3k2rsajjmgnn0tpvr@google.com
CREATED:20170814T203903Z
DESCRIPTION:The Kalamazoo Innovative Initiative is proud to announce our th
 ird meetup of Kalamazoo Inventors Network. This month's guest speaker will 
 cover crowdfunding.\n\nCrowdfunding offers many decisions: Which type of cr
 owdfunding? Which type of platform? What will investors think of me?\n\nTho
 mas Coke\, a former securities regulator and crowdfunding attorney will pre
 sent an overview of the crowdfunding landscape\, including history\, types 
 of crowdfunding\, and test cases on best practices in the crowdfunding spac
 e for companies. \n\nBring questions and prepare for a conversation as much
  as a presentation.\n\nThomas Coke is a lawyer and startup advisor. He is t
 he CEO if a collegiate crowdfunding company\, CampusStarter\, as well as th
 e former VP of North America for Hubbub\, a UK based crowdfunding company. 
 Prior to that he was with CrowdFundConnect and Director of Business Develop
 ment and Compliance\, and with VerifyValid\, both of which were startups th
 at exited. He cut his teeth as a securities regulator and attorney for the 
 State of Michigan Securities Division and has helped write several state cr
 owdfunding bills and speaks around the Midwest on crowdfunding and startup 
 finance\, including teach at CMU in their new MET program.\n\n\nLet's conti
 nue to work together in turning ideas into useful and innovative products a
 nd services for our community.
