CREATED:20170926T235536Z
DESCRIPTION:Makers (***) will learn various tips and techniques for creatin
 g structures from cardboard and hot glue\, including cutting and shaping yo
 ur board. Supplies will be provided. Group will work on and keep an individ
 ual project.\n\nSome skills that can be learned:\n\n-Why is cardboard and h
 ot glue so great?\n\n-Measuring and cutting your cardboard\n\n-Understandin
 g the corrugation/grain of the cardboard\n\n-Techniques for cutting cardboa
 rd (using a ruler to cut against\, using a drawn line)\n\n-Techniques for f
 olding cardboard with accuracy-Curving cardboard uniformly\n\n-Techniques f
 or using hot glue (and working with it before it cools)\n\n-Basic engineeri
 ng with cardboard-Safety using paper\, hot glue\, and razor cutters\n\nLIMI
 T OF 8 PEOPLE\n\nRSVP at https://www.meetup.com/KzooMakers/events/243693780
 /\n\nCost - $10/members $15 - non-members\n\nFor a complete listing of even
 ts\, please visit http://kzoomakers.org/events-calendar/\n\n\n***This event
  centers around the use of sharp and hot tools with large body movement and
  focused concentration. Individuals will be responsible for their own safet
 y as well as those who may be impacted by their crafting. Safety while usin
 g these tools will be featured.
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T101557Z
LOCATION:Kzoo Makers\, 1102 E Michigan Ave\, Kalamazoo\, MI\, Kalamazoo\, M
 I 49048\, USA\, Meeting Area
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Creating Structures with Cardboard
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
