DESCRIPTION:Imagine you found an electronic kit you want to build and all t
 he parts you need came with it. But which one is a resistor\, let alone the
  47k R1 or the 2.2k R2 the instructions "talk" about? And what about a capa
 citor\, an LED or something called an NE555? And what do those nice colored
  rings around some parts and the small numbers on others mean? How do you i
 dentify each part so you can put it in the correct location? Join us on Mon
 day October 2nd at 6:30 PM at KzooMakers and find out. \n\nThis workshop wi
 ll help you identify components\, read their values and learn a little abou
 t their functions. \n\nIt is free to KzooMakers members and $5 for non-memb
 ers.\n\nFor a complete listing of events please visit https://kzoomakers.or
 g/events-calendar/
