UID:34ckhi3gpvl6hgr1onjlepknkt@google.com
CREATED:20171006T001812Z
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is going to be much more hands-on\, we will be ta
 lking about and using Switches and starting to get a full view on how simpl
 e circuits work. We will be using Resistors\, LED’s\, and switches that are
  all on the Electronics Learning Lab kit. This allows us to work without ha
 ving to use extensions and messy setups. Things we will cover during this w
 orkshop: Basic switch use and type\, Ohms Law\, and using a volt meter. We 
 may talk about some basic power considerations as well but more detail on t
 hat should be part of Workshop 3.  Please review the Radioshack ELL workboo
 k from pages 1-18 (available from QSL.NET at this link <http://www.qsl.net/
 k/kb1uif/downloads/Docs/Tutorials/2800280_P1_PM_EN.pdf> ). \n\nIf you didn'
 t attend Part 1\, you can catch up by reading the ELL workbook as mentioned
  above.  \n\nIf you  attended Part 1\, this workshop is free to members of 
 KzooMakers and $5 for non-members.  If you did not attend Part 1\, there is
  an additional $5 fee for the Part 1 resource kit (parts and study material
 ) for a total of $5 for members and $10 for non-members. There will be an o
 ptional 'Part 2 supplemental resource kit' available for $5 with some switc
 hes\, assorted resistors and other parts if you want it. If you have a mult
 imeter please bring it
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T101234Z
LOCATION:Kzoo Makers\, 1102 E Michigan Ave\, Kalamazoo\, MI\, Kalamazoo\, M
 I 49048\, USA\, Meeting Area
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Introduction to Electronic Circuits: Part 2
TRANSP:OPAQUE
