DESCRIPTION:<p>Are you eating snacks on plates? ....Like a <em>peasant</em>
 ?</p><p>Come check out our woodshop. You’ll get a brief overview of how som
 e of our tools work then we'll put together a fancy serving tray out of har
 dwood\, with a resin "river" center. We'll have a few colors to choose from
 .</p><p>This class will take place in two sessions to allow time for the re
 sin to cure. The first day (Friday) will be assembly/the resin pour and the
  second (Sunday) will be flattening and finishing.</p><p>Cutting board lase
 r etching is done at another event\, with many designs/personalizations. Ad
 ditional items are available to purchase after event.</p><p><strong>General
  Public</strong><br>$115 - 1 Ticket<br>$140 - 2 People\, 1 Board<br>$185 - 
 2 Tickets\, 2 Boards</p><p><strong>Kzoo Makers Members</strong><br>$105 - 1
  Ticket<br>$130 - 2 People\, 1 Board<br>$175 - 2 Tickets\, 2 Boards</p><p><
 br><b><u>GET TICKETS HERE! </u></b><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ma
 ke-and-take-resin-river-serving-board-tickets-1126317238179">https://www.ev
 entbrite.com/e/make-and-take-resin-river-serving-board-tickets-112631723817
 9</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250307T145933Z
LOCATION:Kzoo Makers\, 1102 E Michigan Ave\, Kalamazoo\, MI 49048\, USA\, W
 ood Shop
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Make and Take: Resin River Serving Boards - Day 2 of 2
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20171011T220000Z
DTEND:20171011T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260305T101422Z
UID:0njnj88vushcsugc6eaura48rv@google.com
CREATED:20170926T175226Z
DESCRIPTION:The Kalamazoo Innovative Initiative is proud to announce our fo
 urth meetup of Kalamazoo Inventors Network. This month's guest speaker will
  cover intellectual property.\n\nCome see this free presentation by Dr. Cla
 rk Bennett as he covers several areas about protecting your ideas? \nPatent
 s vs.Trade Marks. \nWhen should I create a prototype? \nWhat steps can I do
  it myself? \nWhat should I expect when dealing with USPTO?\n\nDr. Bennett 
 has 25 years of intellectual property (IP-patents) management and 10 years 
 of business development and licensing experience gained during his tenure a
 t several companies and Western Michigan University. This experience includ
 es management of a portfolio of 140 patents and founding a start-up company
 . Since 2011\, he has worked in Technology and Innovation Advancement (TIA 
 - TTO office) at WMU\, as Director of TIA since 2013. Previous to this\, Dr
 . Bennett managed IP (patents and trademarks)\, business activities and con
 tract manufacturing at the human therapeutics\, start-up company\, OtoMedic
 ine. In addition\, he was IP and Project Manager with the Pfizer Animal Hea
 lth Company\, where he managed drug and vaccine R&D projects\, and the vacc
 ine patent portfolio. Before Pfizer\, he joined a small 5-person biotech co
 mpany\, IBEX\, where he managed the Molecular and Cellular Biology Laborato
 ries and the company’s patent portfolio\, while conducting biochemical and 
 cell biology research. He helped grow IBEX to 50 researchers before joining
  Pfizer. His research experience also includes positions as a Research Chem
 ist with the USDA-Agricultural Research Service at the University of Illino
 is\, Champaign\, as an NSF Postdoctoral Molecular Biologist at the Universi
 ty of California\, Berkeley\, and as a NIH Pre-doctoral Grant Awardee at Pu
 rdue University. \n\n\nLet's continue to work together in turning ideas int
 o useful and innovative products and services for our community.\n\nFor a c
 omplete listing of events please visit https://kzoomakers.org/events-calend
 ar/
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T101604Z
LOCATION:Kzoo Makers\, 1102 E Michigan Ave\, Kalamazoo\, MI\, Kalamazoo\, M
 I 49048\, USA\, Meeting Area
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kalamazoo Inventors Network presents Dr. Clark Bennett
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
