DESCRIPTION:In this session we will learn about microcontrollers and the Ar
 duino platform.<br><br><br>We will talk about what comprises a microcontrol
 ler and what it can do.<br><br>Then we will discuss the Arduino\, which exp
 ands on the basic microcontroller by implementing an open-source electronic
 s platform or board and the software used to make it simple to program.<br>
 <br>We will cover the basic components on an Arduino board and how this can
  be connected to various inputs (sensors) and outputs (displays or actuator
 s).<br><br>Finally we will see what a simple Adruino program looks like and
  how to load it into the Arduino and see it run.<br><br>We intend to have f
 ollow-on sessions on the first Monday of each month to explore the Arduino 
 in more depth.<br><br>This first workshop is free and limited to 6 KzooMake
 rs members.<br>If you have an arduino\, you are encouraged to bring it.&nbs
 p\;<br>Arduino's($10)\, Arduino project kits($50) and other related items w
 ill be available for purchase at the workshop\, please bring cash.<br><br>F
 or questions\, contact <a href="mailto:ronald.schubot@kzoomakers.org" targe
 t="_blank">ronald.schubot@kzoomakers.org</a>  <br><br><br>RSVP: <a href="ht
 tps://www.meetup.com/KzooMakers/events/tbjfgpyxdbhb/" target="_blank" id="o
 w344" __is_owner="true">https://www.meetup.com/KzooMakers/events/tbjfgpyzdb
 gb/</a><br><br>For a complete listing of all Kzoo Makers events\, please vi
 sit <a href="http://kzoomakers.org/events-calendar/" target="_blank">http:/
 /kzoomakers.org/events-calendar/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T101424Z
LOCATION:Kzoo Makers\, 1102 E Michigan Ave\, Kalamazoo\, MI\, Kalamazoo\, M
 I 49048\, USA\, Meeting Area
SEQUENCE:5
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Electronics Forum: Introduction to Arduino and Microcontrollers (Me
 mbers only)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
