UID:543i0idafmnoih1g2gfjljrhv4@google.com
CREATED:20170830T170804Z
DESCRIPTION:This workshop series will introduce you to electronic circuits.
  In this first workshop you will be introduced to the components used in el
 ectronic circuits such as resistors\, capacitors\, diodes\, Light Emitting 
 Diodes (LEDs)\, transistors\, and integrated circuits. You will also be int
 roduced to reading a simple schematic\, a diagram that describes an electro
 nics circuit\, and use it to build a timer circuit to flash an LED. \n\nThi
 s workshop has a fee of $5 for members and $10 for non-members and you will
  get printed material\, a 400 point solderless breadboard\, jumper wires an
 d parts  needed to build the circuit that you get to keep.\n\nLimited to 10
  people\; members will have priority for the 10  slots
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T101301Z
LOCATION:1102 E Michigan Ave\, Kalamazoo\, MI 49048\, USA\, Meeting Area
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Introduction to Electronic Circuits: Part 1
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
