CREATED:20180120T184059Z
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop we will use the Adruino Experimenter’s guide (
 ARDX) which will guide us through installing the Arduino IDE (development e
 nvironment)\, a small electronics primer\, a small programming primer and t
 hen we will start to program the Arduino.  Experiments include: blinking on
 e LED then 8 LEDs\, spin a motor using a transistor\, control a servo\, con
 trol 8 LEDs using a shift register and more. I am not sure how far we will 
 get in this session but follow-on sessions will proceed through the guide.\
 n\nFor this workshop you will need an Arduino\, an Arduino UNO is what is d
 epicted in the guide\, but other models should work including clones. We wi
 ll also use a solderless breadboard\, jumpers\, and various electronic comp
 onents. If you do not have an Arduino\, I have compatible boards available 
 for $10. Breadboard and jumpers and electronic components will be available
  to use or purchase along with a full experimenters guide kit with all comp
 onents for $45 (usually $50).\n\nWe will be using the Computer labs compute
 rs\, but if you have a windows computer you want to use with your arduino\,
  bring it and you can install the software and use that instead. I can only
  help with installing on windows\, if you use Mac or Linux please research 
 installing the Arduino IDE on your platform before the session. You will al
 so need to download the CH340/341 USB serial drivers for your version of OS
  if they are not included. I believe current versions of windows and Linux 
 already support the CH340\, I do not know about OSX. If you have questions 
 please contact me.\n\nThis workshop is only open to KzooMakers paid members
  and there is a $5 fee which includes a printed manual. If you also need an
  Arduino\, the cost will be $15 ($5+$10). Please bring cash for any purchas
 es. Non members can contact me and if there are any open seats\, you may be
  able to attend for a slightly higher price.\n\nInformation on ARDX can be 
 found at oomlout.com\, click on the ‘oomlout’ then select ARDX to see the e
 xperiments. You can search for ‘Adruino Experimenter’s guide (ARDX)’ to fin
 d a pdf of the guide.\n\n\nRSVP: https://www.meetup.com/KzooMakers/events/t
 bjfgpyzfbgb/\n\nFor a complete listing of all Kzoo Makers events\, please v
 isit http://kzoomakers.org/events-calendar/
LAST-MODIFIED:20221210T101424Z
LOCATION:Kzoo Makers\, 1102 E Michigan Ave\, Kalamazoo\, MI\, Kalamazoo\, M
 I 49048\, USA\, Meeting Area
SEQUENCE:5
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Electronics Forum:  Adruino Experimenters guide – Making it do some
 thing!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
